* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.png binary

# The generated cross-language lifecycle contract (#612). Every other generated
# target is already pinned by extension (.py, .json, .md); this was the only one
# that was not, so with core.autocrlf=true it checked out as CRLF while the
# generator writes LF. The drift check compares decoded text, so it passed, and
# `generate` skips a write whose decoded text already matches -- a byte-level
# change to the browser contract was therefore neither detected nor repairable.
# Pinned narrowly rather than pinning all *.js, which would renormalise files
# belonging to unrelated work.
vesta/assets/web/generated-lifecycle.js text eol=lf
vesta/assets/web/vendor/markdown-it-14.1.0.min.js -text
vesta/assets/web/vendor/markdown-it.LICENSE.txt text eol=lf
